"Daniel Nilsson" <daniel@daniel-nilsson.com> wrote 

This is kinda spoily. Fair warning.

> The castle wand has 2 wishes, what should I wish for?

You look like you're pretty well kitted out. I'd get a magic marker
and save the other for an emergency.

> What things should I have with me after the castle?

About what you're carrying. Make sure you have a method of setting
yourself on fire nearby (scroll, wand, or horn), but inside the BoH is
fine. I prefer a wand, since it can be useful for engraving.

> What things should I not have with me?

See below.

> What things are good to have outside the BoH (for fast access)?

Pretty much the stuff you have. I usually keep a / o' teleport in main
inventory, though, and a / o' death if I don't have the finger.

> What scrolls are good for blanking (or the inverse; what scrolls to not
> blank)?

That's a tough call. It's up to you.

> What potions are good for diluting (or the inverse)?

Ditto.

> Other things I should think of when going down into gehennom (I know about
> not praying)?

Watch out for green P's.

> Inventory:
> "oLS

I've rarely found these useful unless worn. By the time you need it,
it's generally too late. I'd save the weight and be careful.

> "oR (being worn)
> Eye of the Aethiopica
> +2 Magicbane
> +4 Hawaiian shirt
> +5 GDSM (from early throne wish)
> fireproof burnt +2 robe (minetown priest's)

(Can't be done. It's either fireproof or burnt.)

> fireproof +2 GoD (from wish in the quest)
> fireproof +1 small shield
> fireproof +5 curnuthaum
> fireproof +4 speed boots
> +3 ring of gain strength

This ring may not be optimal. I like to increase damage, but warning,
automatic searching, or somesuch may be handy. It's not _bad_, though.

> ring of free action
> lizard corpse
> /oCancel
> blessed BoH
> blindfold
> blessed unihorn
> stethoscope
> Bell of Opening (0:2) (accidentally used it once)

No need to haul it around. I'd stash that.

> blessed luckstone

> In BoH:
> the original +1 quarterstaff

A wiz shouldn't need an emergency backup weapon. Stash it.

> ww boots
> mummy wrapping

Probably not necessary if you have teleport and control.

> ring of conflict
> ring of regeneration

I've found that if you need regeneration, it's too late to dig out the
ring. I'd stash it.

> ring of sustain ability

No great need to carry that around, and I've rarely found sustain
ability to be useful anyway. Stash.

> Many scrolls (including blessed charging & genocide)

I usually only keep some teleport scrolls handy, especially cursed
ones. Charging might not hurt to fill up your power in a pinch.

> Good collection of potions

I typically just keep holy water, and maybe a paralysis. If you're
nervous, full healing can be handy.

> Lots of food

By now, you shouldn't need much food. Keep a small stash for
emergencies and live off the land. I usually keep a food ration or
two, plus a blessed tin of spinach. I often keep the tin main
inventory, but it isn't really necessary.

> Many wands (including death, wishing)

You probably don't need that many. I usually keep a wand of wishing, a
wand of fire, and a wand of digging or two around, plus my main
inventory wands.

> tinning kit (for those annoying trolls)
> can of grease

Probably not necessary, unless you're totally paranoid about flayers
or really enjoy fixing squeaky boards. I usually grease my bag,
helmet, and cloak, and stash the grease.

> camera

Useless unless in main inventory. Stash.

> oil lamp (no magic lamps found!)

Too bad about the magic lamp. I'd ditch this and just cast light.

> pick-axe

Wands of digging and/or the dig spell are typically enough, although
in Gehennom sometimes I'll resort to a pick-axe. It won't _hurt_, but
it is heavy.

> about 50 identified gems

Stash. You don't need these at hand. Pick 'em up on your way out, if
you have room.

> blessed luckstone

Stash. Magicbane'll help you avoid getting cursed. On the odd chance
that your luckstone gets burned, just whip some holy water outta your
bag and fix it.

> Some other random junk I picked up.

Stash it or dump it as needed.

Given the chance, I bless everything in my main inventory, although
it's not necessary.

Good luck!

